   "text": {
    "L1": "A bank has three useful jobs: it accepts deposits, gives loans, and helps with payments.",
    "L2": "Here is a common myth: a bank keeps your exact notes in a locker and does nothing else with them.",
    "L3": "That is not true. A bank keeps part as a reserve and lends the rest to people and businesses.",
    "L4": "Your savings can help someone build a house or start a business. The bank pays depositors interest and charges borrowers a higher interest rate.",
    "L5": "A savings account lets you withdraw anytime. A fixed deposit locks money for a fixed period, while a recurring deposit saves a fixed amount each month.",
    "L6": "Simple interest equals principal times rate times time divided by one hundred.",
    "L7": "For ₹5,000 at 8% per year for 2 years, the interest is ₹800 and the total is ₹5,800.",
    "L8": "Now check the idea: which account lets you withdraw your money anytime?"
   },
